      {
        "id": 2757,
        "name": "Snoopy and the Red Baron",
        "summary": "The dastardly Red Baron has stolen important food supplies from the allies during the war. Hamburgers, ice cream cones, popcorn and other tasty treats have been taken by this evil aviator and sharpshooter. Your task is to help Snoopy shoot down the Red Baron and recover the stolen supplies.\n\nYou begin your mission with four doghouses. It takes eight direct hits to bring down the Red Baron, and for the Red baron to bring down Snoopy's doghouse. If the Red Baron downs a doghouse, all accumulated treats will be lost. Press the controller button to fire Snoopy's machine gun.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co7x7d.jpg",
        "release_date": 441676800,
        "rating": 48.0,
        "rating_count": 5,
        "genres": "Shooter,Arcade",
        "platform_ids": "59",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/snoopy-and-the-red-baron",
        "cached_at": 1778663163
      },
      {
        "id": 3252,
        "name": "Alpha Beam With Ernie",
        "summary": "The object of Alpha Beam is to help Sesame Street's Ernie pilot a small shuttle, collect fuel tanks (marked by a letter of the alphabet), and return them to his space ship so that he can return to Earth.\n\nThe game was marketed as a family-friendly game that could teach children pre-reading skills such as identifying and matching letters. Alpha Beam was compatible with the Atari Kid's Controller, which was sold separately, although the regular keyboard controller is also compatible",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/ojbeq5xgccvzhrfff7nz.jpg",
        "release_date": 439084800,
        "rating": null,
