      {
        "id": 6706,
        "name": "E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial",
        "summary": "E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial (also referred to simply as E.T.) is a 1982 adventure video game developed and published by Atari, Inc. for the Atari 2600 video game console. It is based on the film of the same name, and was designed by Howard Scott Warshaw. The objective of the game is to guide the eponymous character through various screens to collect three pieces of an interplanetary telephone that will allow him to contact his home planet. It is widely regarded as the worst game ever made and one of the major contributing factors to the near death of the video game industry in 1983.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co94rk.jpg",
        "release_date": 407548800,
        "rating": 48.10090533775946,
        "rating_count": 42,
        "genres": "Strategy,Adventure",
        "platform_ids": "59",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/e-t-the-extra-terrestrial",
        "cached_at": 1778663163
      },
      {
        "id": 6881,
        "name": "Assault",
        "summary": "A mothership drops aliens, up to three on screen at a time. There are ten per level. You must shoot them but avoid the items they fire at you. You fire by pushing up on the joystick. Pushing left or right makes you go left or right. If you hold down the button, pushing left or right makes you fire left or right. Later enemies will drop fireballs that chase you along the ground or split in two smaller enemies when shot. If you fire non-stop, you will build up heat as indicated by the green bar at the bottom right. If you overheat or are hit by an enemy, you loser a life. The game is over when you lose all lives or reach a score of 999,999. You get a new man (4 max) every 10,000 points.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co9n46.jpg",
        "release_date": 441676800,
        "rating": null,
        "rating_count": null,
        "genres": "Shooter,Arcade",
        "platform_ids": "59",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/assault",
        "cached_at": 1778663163
      },
      {
        "id": 8253,
        "name": "Adventure",
        "summary": "Adventure is a video game for the Atari 2600 video game console, released in 1980. In the game, the player controls a square avatar whose quest is to hunt an open world environment for a magical chalice, returning it to the golden castle. The game world is populated by roaming enemies: dragons, which can eat the avatar; and a bat, which randomly steals and hides items around the game world.\n\nAdventure was designed and programmed by Atari employee Warren Robinett, and published by Atari, Inc. At the time, Atari programmers were generally given full control on the creative direction and development cycle for their games, and this required them to plan for their next game as they neared completion of their current one to stay productive.\n\nRobinett submitted the source code for Adventure to Atari management in June 1979 and soon left Atari. Atari released the game in early 1980.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co69tb.jpg",
        "release_date": 347068800,
        "rating": 76.44882391804732,
        "rating_count": 41,
        "genres": "Adventure",
        "platform_ids": "59",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/adventure",
        "cached_at": 1778663163
      },
      {
        "id": 8466,
        "name": "Cosmic Ark",
        "summary": "The sun of Alpha Ro is fading fast! Soon it will flicker out. The Cosmic Ark races to save creatures from doomed planets in that solar system. Meteor showers bombard the Ark, threatening its Atlantean crew - and planetary defense systems make this mission of mercy doubly treacherous! Time and energy slip away- work fast or these defenceless little beasties will disappear for all time.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co9j0w.jpg",
        "release_date": 410140800,
        "rating": 65.73903608655668,
        "rating_count": 6,
        "genres": "Shooter,Arcade",
        "platform_ids": "59",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/cosmic-ark",
        "cached_at": 1778663163
      },
      {
        "id": 8529,
        "name": "Custer's Revenge",
        "summary": "You are General Custer. Your dander's up, your pistol's wavin‘. You've set your sights on a ravishing maiden named Revenge: but she's not about to take it lying down, by George! Help is on the way. If you're to get to Revenge you'll have to rise to the challenge, dodge a tribe of flying arrows and protect your flanks against some downright mean and prickly cactus. But if you can stand pat and last post the stings and arrows - you can stand last.\n\nRemember! Revenge is sweet. Everytime ol' Custer scores he comes up smilin‘ and right back for more. The higher the score. the more challenging the game action gets.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/ax0ftquzccrc1kb11xjo.jpg",
        "release_date": 401587200,
        "rating": 20.84574218188036,
        "rating_count": 6,
        "genres": "Arcade",
        "platform_ids": "59",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/custers-revenge",
        "cached_at": 1778663163
      },
      {
        "id": 10203,
        "name": "Star Wars: Jedi Arena",
        "summary": "In Jedi Arena, you have to face an opponent in the arena to see who is the true Jedi master. Wandering throughout the arena is a seeker which is capable of firing laser bolts. To be victorious you need to destroy your opponents shield by having the seeker fire laser bolts at it. You are armed only with a light saber which is used to control the direction of the laser bolts you fire, as well as block incoming fire from your opponent.\n\nThe first player to break through the other players shield wins a point, and the first player to 3 points wins the match! Several game options are included which control the speed of the seeker, or even make the seeker invisible.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co74j8.jpg",
        "release_date": 412905600,
        "rating": 59.89336502554637,
        "rating_count": 7,
        "genres": "Fighting",
        "platform_ids": "59",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/star-wars-jedi-arena",
        "cached_at": 1778663163
      },
      {
        "id": 10205,
        "name": "Star Wars: Return of the Jedi - Ewok Adventure",
        "summary": "Star Wars: Return of the Jedi - Ewok Adventure, also known as Revenge of the Jedi: Game I is a cancelled 1983 shoot 'em up video game based on the Star Wars: Return of the Jedi film. The game was developed by Atari Games and to be published by Parker Brothers on the Atari 2600, Atari 7800, ColecoVision, and Intellivision video game consoles.\n\nAlthough it was completed, the game was never released for sale, as the marketing department of Parker Brothers considered the controls too difficult to master. A prototype cartridge surfaced in the early 2000s.\n\nIn Ewok Adventure, the player takes the role of an Ewok in the hang glider corps with the mission to destroy a shield generator of the Imperial army. The player can control a hang glider with the joystick and has to evade enemies. Depending on the game mode, the player can either make the hang glider climb and decent by pulling back and forth the joystick, or he can reverse the vertical directions. Hitting the ground results in a game over. Furthermore, the player can pick up rocks to drop on enemies when flying over them.\n\nOnly one physical copy of Ewok Adventure is currently known to exist. Larry Gelberg, designer of the game, gave the only known prototype of the game to his son in the early 2000s, who later sold the game for $1,680.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co1piv.jpg",
        "release_date": null,
        "rating": null,
        "rating_count": null,
        "genres": "Shooter,Arcade",
        "platform_ids": "68,60,59,67",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/star-wars-return-of-the-jedi-ewok-adventure",
        "cached_at": 1778663163
      },
      {
        "id": 11113,
        "name": "Air Raid",
        "summary": "Air Raid is considered to be the rarest game released for the Atari 2600.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co7xu5.jpg",
        "release_date": 410140800,
        "rating": null,
